        "abstract": "It is suggested that by the use of a three-terminal device a practical means for the application of the required high electric field can be obtained. A novel quantum well with Bragg structure, useful for electric field-effect wavelength tuning, is proposed to reduce the screening effect. As in the case of the guided modes in a Bragg reflection waveguide, bound electronic states can exist in a quantum well structure with a semi-infinite periodic medium instead of a usual potential barrier. Since the bound state is very sensitive to the composite structure the energy level can easily be changed by varying the applied field. As a result, large range wavelength tunability can be achieved.<<ETX xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">&gt;</ETX>",
